G0482.d:
ἀντι-λαμβάνω
[frequently in LXX for חָזַק hi., סָמַךְ, etc ;]
to take instead of or in turn. Mid., with genitive, to take hold of;
(a) of persons, to help (see MM, VGT, see word): Luk.1:54, Act.20:35;
(b) of things, to partake of: 1Ti.6:2 (see Field, Notes, 210; Cremer, 386; and cf. συν-αντιλαμβάνω).†
(AS)

G0468.d:
ἀντ-από-δομα, -τος, τό
(ἀνταποδίδωμι) [in LXX chiefly for גְּמוּל ;] ( = cl. -δοσις, which see)
requital;
(a) in favourable sense: Luk.14:12;
(b) in unfavourable sense: Rom.11:9.†
(AS)

G0467.d:
ἀντ-απο-δίδωμι
(ἀντί ἀποδίδωμι), [in LXX for שָׁלַם pi., גָּמַל, שׁוּב hi., etc. ;]
to give back as an equivalent, recompense, requital (the ἀντί ex­pressing the idea of full, complete return; see Lft., Notes, 46);
(a) in favourable sense: Luk.14:14, Rom.11:35, 1Th.3:9;
(b) in unfavourable sense: Rom.12:19, 2Th.1:6, Heb.10:30.†
(AS)
